 "description": "<p>On March 7th, it was reported that the ALPHV (BlackCat) ransomware group attacked the Administradora de Subsidios Sociales (ADESS). (adess[.]gob[.]do)&nbsp;</p><p>As a result of the attack, there was an unavailability of some systems hosted on their internal servers.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"/api/v2/hi/threat/f028785d7a4f748adfb68eebe6573f576873565d/file/e0a6068d4c6d6a587abd1f2ace3520b883a977651a522cccce926deebf843f70?placeholder=__IMAGE_:e0a6068d4c6d6a587abd1f2ace3520b883a977651a522cccce926deebf843f70_IMAGE__\" data-mce-src=\"__IMAGE_:e0a6068d4c6d6a587abd1f2ace3520b883a977651a522cccce926deebf843f70_IMAGE__\" /></p><p>As of March 11th, it remains unclear whether the attackers have exfiltrated data from the victim's servers.&nbsp;</p><p>Additionally, the perpetrators have not made any announcements or disclosures on the Data Leaks Site (DLS) concerning the attack on Administradora de Subsidios Sociales (ADESS).</p>",
